cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use this software in academic work, please cite this software.
type: software
title: "flinch: solar flares in Sun-as-a-star radial velocities"
version: 1.0.0
date-released: 2026-11-23
authors:
  - family-names: "García"
    given-names: "Gabriel"
    affiliation: "Universidad Complutense de Madrid"
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0001-7256-2609"
repository-code: https://github.com/gabgarar/flinch
url: https://gabgarar.github.io/flinch/
license: BSD-3-Clause
abstract: >-
  Do solar flares contaminate the radial-velocity detection of Earth analogues? Radial
  velocity of the Sun observed as a star during M- and X-class flares, measured with the
  NEID and HARPS-N solar data and the GOES flare lists, with the response of the
  chromospheric lines in the NEID spectra.
keywords:
  - solar physics
  - solar flares
  - radial velocity
  - Sun-as-a-star
  - exoplanets
  - Earth analogues
  - stellar activity
  - NEID
  - HARPS-N
